<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">itemlevel</ansi>

Item level (1 to 70) is where an item came from: the level of the foe, boss
or chest that produced it. It decides how strong its affixes can be, and
what you need to wear it.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Affix tiers</ansi>

An affix has up to five tiers of strength. Item level opens them:

  Item level   1+      15+      30+      45+      60+
  Tier         1        2        3        4        5

An item always rolls the highest tier its item level allows, with the
number inside that tier's range chosen at random. Reading an item at Scribe
rank 4 shows its affix tiers and ranges.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Tier</ansi>

The tier of the base type (Common, Steel, Tempered, Masterwork, Runeforged
and Relic) is a separate thing: it is the material and the power budget the
item starts with. Tier comes from the type, item level from where it was
found (<ansi fg="command">help equipmenttiers</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">To wear it</ansi>

Rare and better gear needs a character level 5 below its item level;
Uncommon 10 below; Common none (<ansi fg="command">help rarity</ansi>).

See also: <ansi fg="command">help rarity</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help quality</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help affixes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help equipment</ansi>.
